 {"id":"fabro-8275","title":"Downgrade the by-design preamble allow-key absence warn to info","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:17:29.202Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:21:27.438Z","description":"In the preamble fidelity module of fabro-workflow, the warn 'preamble_allow_keys entry absent … key=output.gate_known_bug_hits' fired on a green first-visit stage of develop run 01M1YGJ7JSWAVWJT45DRDZ89Z6, even though key absence on first visit is by design and fires on every clean run. Change: emit info (not warn) when an allow-listed context key is absent on a node's first visit; keep warn for repeat visits or genuine contract regressions. Expected effect: warn-level logs stop crying wolf on every green run while real fidelity regressions stay visible. Related but distinct from fabro-meta-c454 (input-contract closure, not log level).\nBasis: run 01M1YGJ7JSWAVWJT45DRDZ89Z6, workflow version 4ff76f32665f954e9a8e2027ec2a4a5b48266707730ae0620fcfd3f79acd4a10, commit f7126d9612d28110fca518d3aeeeb941bd7b659d","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-22e4","title":"agent: edit-tool file writes land with mtime 1970-01-01 — cargo skips recompiles, edits silently lag until manual touch","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.569Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.569Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"From unreviewed run 01M1Y2SMEVDHAFB59GZV9B84CQ (PR #41 implementer; recovered via journal sweep 2026-09-07 after the run aged out of revisor freshness): edit-tool file writes landed with mtime 1970-01-01 (e.g. lib/components/fabro-validate/src/file_refs.rs), so cargo considered the sources older than cached rlibs and silently skipped recompiles — a just-added pub fn was reported missing and behavior lagged the edits until a manual touch. This is silent cache poisoning of the build loop: any agent edit can produce a stale-binary diagnosis that costs implementer revisits. Fix direction: the platform's file-write path (edit tool / sandbox write transport) must set a real mtime — utimensat/write-with-times after creating or replacing the file so downstream build systems see fresh sources. Acceptance: an edit-tool write produces mtime == wall clock (unit test on the write path); a before/after cargo check in a scratch crate recompiles after an agent edit without manual touch.","labels":["engine","agent"]}
